From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:42:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 392/394] wifi: mediatek: add the MT6797 WLAN driver

Add the WLAN function of the MT6797 connectivity subsystem as two
modules:
- mt6797-wlan-core: the AHB host interface with its INIT and normal
  command transport, the firmware container parser and section
  transfer, and the post-start record preparation;
- mac: a mac80211 managed-mode station, split into main.c
  (registration, mac80211 operations, scan, regulatory), join.c (the
  station lifetime: join, association, data pump, teardown and re-arm)
  and data.c (transmit PIDs and rates, checked CCMP receive with host PN
  validation, receive reordering and connection monitoring).

The behaviour is the development station's: WPA2-PSK with
firmware-owned encryption, HT40 with receive A-MPDU, data at a fixed HT
MCS5, or at mac80211's rate control with the rate_control module
parameter, and automatic reconnects. Known limits: scan, join and
receive are pinned to channel 40, the scan is passive, there is no
group-key rekey and no power save, and receive is polled.

This replaces the station's Wi-Fi patches. Compared with them:
- the 48 experiment Kconfig switches are folded to the station's values
  and the branches they left dead are removed (checkpoint 0389, which
  ran on the station);
- the test schedule, snapshots, records and host-test shims are removed;
- the unused image-binding and EMI helper layers are dropped;
- the single-use helper headers are merged into the files that use them
  and the mac80211 layer is split into three files without changing the
  moved code;
- the transmit data depth is folded at 12, an unreachable channel-token
  wrap refusal is removed, and checkpatch fixes add two small helpers.
